{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791542717,"nonce":"cucXfPSn5k0zh0MoApG9uOxs+nM=","title":"Reflected anonymous Array fields discard their element layout","message":"At 94d14e941e8ad43a221f4996caa1ffe5639e60f8, Issue5293 and Issue9372 lose String/integer element types in template foreach loops. Preserving array boxes through iterator construction fixes direct Dynamic array loops but leaves the template failures: anonymous field descriptors carry only the Array tag, so Reflect.field reboxes the raw array with layout zero.\n\nCarry the Array element layout alongside anonymous field types. Include it in compiler-emitted shape descriptors, preserve it when fields promote to map storage, and update it when Reflect.setField replaces an array. Reuse the existing array-boxing layout codec. DynamicArrayIteration covers reflected fields, map promotion, deletion, replacement, shape retyping, and template iteration. The linked iterator issue is bae2dc4bf7164b858f23972a65bb5b4b2a30aeca60579100c5f170e9d2584e40. Full validation pending.","files":null}]}